  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Radhaben Kumar Lal Tahalyani vs State Of Rajasthan on 21 January, 2019 High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Miscellaneous (Petition) No. 374/2019 Radhaben Kumar Lal Tahalyani & Ors. ----Petitioners Versus State Of Rajasthan & Anr. ----Respondents For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Ajay Tanwar for Mr. Ashvin Garg For Respondent(s) : Ms. Meenakshi Pareek, Pp Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Kanwaljit Singh Ahluwalia Order 21/01/2019",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the petitioners has contended that sample of turmeric powder was taken from the premises M/ . Counsel for the petitioners has contended that petitioners are the partners of a firm and fall in the category of 'Manufacturer'. Counsel for the petitioners has contended that on 12.08.1998 report of State Public Health Laboratory was received and on basis thereof complaint was filed on 04.04.2001. Counsel for the petitioners has contended that it was specifically written on the wrapper of the turmeric powder that its expiry date is 01.11.1998.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Counsel for the petitioners has contended that sample of turmeric powder was taken from the premises M/ . Counsel for the petitioners has contended that petitioners are the partners of a firm and fall in the category of 'Manufacturer'. Counsel for the petitioners has contended that on 12.08.1998 report of State Public Health Laboratory was received and on basis thereof complaint was filed on 04.04.2001. Counsel for the petitioners has contended that it was specifically written on the wrapper of the turmeric powder that its expiry date is 01.11.1998.",
